<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Q1 real GDP rises 1.5 pct yr/yr (+4.6 pct).</title>
<headline>Czech Q1 real GDP rises 1.5 pct yr/yr (+4.6 pct).</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech first quarter gross domestic product, in real terms, rose 1.5 percent over the same period in 1996, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>GDP growth for the first quarter of 1996 was 4.6 percent, year-on-year.  </p>
<p> CZECH GDP (in CZK bln)	   Q1 97    Q4 96  Q1-Q4 96  Q1 96</p>
<p>  real amount			 268.9    356.9   1,247.0  264.9</p>
<p>  household demand		  145.7    174.1     634.7  138.2</p>
<p>  public-sector demand	     62.2     78.8     275.1   62.9</p>
<p>  gross creation/ fixed capital  71.0    153.9     442.0   69.7</p>
<p>  chg stock/reserves		 22.7    -11.6	23.6   15.8</p>
<p>  exports goods/services	  169.2    196.3     725.2  167.6</p>
<p>  imports goods/services	  201.9    234.6     853.6  189.3</p>
<p>Note. All figures, calculated in real terms, are in billions of crowns. All 1996 figures are revised.  </p>
<p> CZECH GDP (in pct)		    Q1 97</p>
<p>  real change yr/yr		     1.5</p>
<p>  household demand			5.4</p>
<p>  public-sector demand		 -1.1</p>
<p>  gross creation/fixed capital	1.9</p>
<p>  chg stock/reserves		   43.7</p>
<p>  exports goods/services		1.0</p>
<p>  imports goods/services		6.7</p>
<p>  effective household demand	  3.0</p>
<p>  aggregate effective demand	  2.2</p>
<p>Note. All figures are in real, percentage terms. The CSU did not release revised percentage figures for any period of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
